1
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:34,800
A universe without boundaries needs heroes without limits.

2
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:03,600
Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets is a adventure,
science fiction, action film directed by Luc Besson.

3
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:32,400
In the 28th century, Valerian and Laureline are special operatives
charged with keeping order throughout the human territories.

4
00:21:55,200 --> 00:22:01,200
On assignment from the Minister of Defense, the two undertake a mission to Alpha, an ever-expanding metropolis where
species from across the universe have converged over centuries to share knowledge, intelligence, and cultures.

5
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:30,000
At the center of Alpha is a mysterious dark force which threatens the peaceful existence of the City of a Thousand Planets, and
Valerian and Laureline must race to identify the menace and safeguard not just Alpha, but the future of the universe.

6
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:58,800
Valerian, played by Dane DeHaan.

7
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:27,599
Laureline, played by Cara Delevingne.

8
00:43:50,400 --> 00:43:56,400
Commander Arün Filitt, played by Clive Owen.

9
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:25,200
Bubble, played by Rihanna.

10
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:54,000
Jolly the Pimp, played by Ethan Hawke.

11
01:00:16,800 --> 01:00:22,800
Defence Minister, played by Herbie Hancock.

12
01:05:45,600 --> 01:05:51,600
Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets (French: Valérian et la Cité des mille planètes) is a 2017 space
opera film written and directed by Luc Besson, and produced by his wife, Virginie Besson-Silla.

13
01:11:14,400 --> 01:11:20,400
It is based on the French science fiction comics series Valérian and Laureline, written by
Pierre Christin, illustrated by Jean-Claude Mézières, and published by Dargaud.

14
01:16:43,199 --> 01:16:49,199
It stars Dane DeHaan and Cara Delevingne as Valerian and Laureline, respectively, with Clive Owen,
Rihanna, Ethan Hawke, Herbie Hancock, Kris Wu and Rutger Hauer in supporting roles.

15
01:22:12,000 --> 01:22:18,000
Besson independently financed and personally funded the film.

16
01:27:40,800 --> 01:27:46,800
With a production budget of around $180 million, it is both the most expensive
European and the most expensive independent film ever made.

17
01:33:09,600 --> 01:33:15,600
The film is a large international co-production between France, the United
States, China, Germany, Belgium, and the United Arab Emirates.

18
01:38:38,400 --> 01:38:44,400
In the film, two operatives of the United Human Federation are on a mission to
Alpha, a city inhabited by thousands of species from different planets.

19
01:44:07,199 --> 01:44:13,199
Their latest mission is to uncover a destructive force beneath the sprawling city,
realizing it threatens not just Alpha, but the entire universe.

20
01:49:36,000 --> 01:49:42,000
Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets was released on 20 July 2017 in Germany by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures under the Buena Vista International imprint, in the United States on 21 July by
STXfilms, in France on 26 July by EuropaCorp Distribution, in China on 25 August by China Film Group, in Belgium on 26 August by Belga Films, and 27 November in United Arab Emirates by Gulf Film.

21
01:55:04,800 --> 01:55:10,800
It received mixed reviews from critics, who criticised the plot
and some of the casting, but praised the visuals.

22
02:00:33,600 --> 02:00:39,600
It grossed $226 million worldwide, but due to its high production and advertising costs,
was considered a box-office bomb following its release in the United States.

23
02:06:02,400 --> 02:06:08,400
The film explores themes of future, shapeshifting,
space travel, utopia, based on comic.

24
02:11:31,200 --> 02:11:37,200
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
